Day 10 – Associate an Elastic IP with an EC2 Instance (AWS)

Objective

The Nautilus DevOps team needs a fixed public IP address for datacenter-ec2. Attach the existing Elastic IP datacenter-ec2-eip to the instance datacenter-ec2 in the us-east-1 region.

Configuration
Setting                  Value
Elastic IP Name          datacenter-ec2-eip
Elastic IP Address       52.205.189.66
Allocation ID            eipalloc-034c38c3cd7c2052f
Instance Name            datacenter-ec2
Instance ID              i-03642055caaadbe17
Instance Type            t2.micro
Availability Zone        us-east-1a
Private IPv4             172.31.94.93

Steps Performed
1. Opened the EC2 Console and went to Network & Security -> Elastic IPs.
2. Selected datacenter-ec2-eip and opened Actions -> Associate Elastic IP address.
3. Set Resource type to Instance and selected i-03642055caaadbe17 (datacenter-ec2).
4. Left the private IP blank, so the Elastic IP attaches to the primary private IP (172.31.94.93).
5. Left "Allow this Elastic IP address to be reassociated" unticked, since the address was not associated with anything else.
6. Clicked Associate and confirmed the banner "Elastic IP address associated successfully" for 52.205.189.66 -> i-03642055caaadbe17.

Important Concepts Learned
- Elastic IP (EIP): A static public IPv4 address that stays with your account until you release it. A normal public IP changes when an instance is stopped and started.
- Association: An EIP can be attached to an instance or to a network interface. Associating an EIP with an instance that already has one replaces the old address, which is then released from the instance but kept in the account.
- Reassociation flag: Prevents an EIP already in use from being moved without a deliberate choice.
- Charges: AWS charges for an EIP that is allocated but not associated with a running instance, so detach or release unused addresses.

Key Takeaway
An Elastic IP gives an instance a stable public address. Associate it with the instance's primary private IP, and keep in mind that unattached EIPs are billed.
